KohlmeyerKruerPartI.lean contains the original base-two proof by
Jensen Kohlmeyer and Liam Kruer, adapted only to the matching local common
definitions. Original source: sources/KohlmeyerKruerPartI.original.lean.

The recurrence construction, counterexample formalization, integration, and
associated exposition were prepared for Jensen Kohlmeyer with Codex assistance
on 10 October 2026. They use the parity mechanism from Jesse Geneson's earlier
universal counterexample and reference the number family discussed by Dubickas
(2006). Neither earlier mathematical priority nor Kitamura's authorship is
claimed for the submitter. See README.md and PROOF.md for the precise scope.

